Create a Task
Creates a new task inside a specified project and returns the newly created task object.
POST /v1/projects/{project_id}/tasks
Base URL: https://api.taskflow.example.com
Authentication: Required (Bearer token)
Rate limit: 100 requests per minute per user

Description
Use this endpoint to add a task to a project. The task must have a title and may optionally include a description, an assignee, a due date, and a priority level. The authenticated user must be a member of the project with permission to create tasks (roles: owner, admin, or member; users with the viewer role cannot create tasks).
If no priority is supplied, the task is created with priority medium. If no assignee_id is supplied, the task is created as unassigned. New tasks always start with the status open.

Request Headers
Header	Type	Required	Description
Authorization	string	Yes	Bearer token identifying the user. Format: Bearer <access_token>.
Content-Type	string	Yes	Must be application/json.
Accept	string	No	Set to application/json. This is the only supported response format.
Idempotency-Key	string	No	A unique value (such as a UUID) up to 64 characters. If you retry a request with the same key within 24 hours, the API returns the original response instead of creating a duplicate task.

Path Parameters
Name	Type	Required	Description
project_id	string	Yes	The unique ID of the project in which to create the task (e.g., prj_8f3a21c9).

Query Parameters
Name	Type	Required	Description
notify_assignee	boolean	No	If true, the assignee receives an email notification about the new task. Defaults to true. Ignored if no assignee is set.

Request Body Parameters
The body must be a JSON object with the following fields.
Name	Type	Required	Constraints	Description
title	string	Yes	1–200 characters; cannot be only whitespace	A short name for the task.
description	string	No	Up to 5,000 characters	A detailed explanation of the work to be done. Plain text or Markdown.
assignee_id	string	No	Must be the ID of an existing member of the project	The user responsible for the task. Omit or set to null for an unassigned task.
due_date	string	No	ISO 8601 date (YYYY-MM-DD); must be today or a future date	The date by which the task should be completed.
priority	string	No	One of low, medium, high. Default: medium	The importance of the task.
Fields not listed above are rejected with a 400 error.

Example Request
POST /v1/projects/prj_8f3a21c9/tasks?notify_assignee=true HTTP/1.1
Host: api.taskflow.example.com
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.example
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 5b1f0c52-3e7a-4d0e-9c1a-2f8a6b7d9e10
Request body:
{
  "title": "Design landing page mockups",
  "description": "Create three desktop and two mobile mockups for the new product landing page. Share drafts in the #design channel for feedback.",
  "assignee_id": "usr_4d92b7e1",
  "due_date": "2026-11-06",
  "priority": "high"
}
cURL equivalent:
curl -X POST "https://api.taskflow.example.com/v1/projects/prj_8f3a21c9/tasks" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ACCESS_TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "title": "Design landing page mockups",
    "assignee_id": "usr_4d92b7e1",
    "due_date": "2026-11-06",
    "priority": "high"
  }'
________________________________________
