Response Fields
Field	Type	Description
id	string	Unique identifier of the new task.
project_id	string	ID of the project the task belongs to.
title	string	The task title.
description	string or null	The task description, or null if none was provided.
status	string	Always open for a newly created task.
priority	string	low, medium, or high.
due_date	string or null	Due date in YYYY-MM-DD format, or null if none was set.
assignee	object or null	Basic details of the assigned user, or null if unassigned.
created_by	object	The user who created the task (the authenticated user).
created_at	string	UTC timestamp of creation (ISO 8601).
updated_at	string	UTC timestamp of the last update (ISO 8601). Equal to created_at on creation.

HTTP Response Codes
Code	Name	When it occurs
201	Created	The task was created successfully. The response body contains the new task.
200	OK	Returned only when a request is repeated with an Idempotency-Key already used within 24 hours. The original task is returned and no new task is created.
400	Bad Request	The request is malformed: the body is not valid JSON, a required field (title) is missing, a field has the wrong data type, priority is not low, medium, or high, due_date is not in YYYY-MM-DD format, or the body contains unrecognized fields.
401	Unauthorized	The Authorization header is missing, the token is malformed, expired, or has been revoked.
403	Forbidden	The token is valid, but the user is not a member of the project or has the viewer role and cannot create tasks.
404	Not Found	No project exists with the given project_id, or the project exists but is not visible to the user.
409	Conflict	The project is archived and no longer accepts new tasks, or an Idempotency-Key was reused with a different request body.
415	Unsupported Media Type	The Content-Type header is missing or is not application/json.
422	Unprocessable Entity	The JSON is well-formed but a value breaks a business rule: assignee_id does not belong to a member of the project, due_date is in the past, title is empty or only whitespace, or a text field exceeds its maximum length.
429	Too Many Requests	The rate limit (100 requests per minute) has been exceeded. Wait for the number of seconds in the Retry-After header, then retry.
500	Internal Server Error	An unexpected error occurred on the server. Retry after a short delay; if the problem persists, contact support with the request_id.
503	Service Unavailable	The service is temporarily down for maintenance or overloaded. Retry later.

Error Response Format
All errors use the same structure:
{
  "error": {
    "code": "validation_failed",
    "message": "The request body contains invalid values.",
    "details": [
      {
        "field": "due_date",
        "issue": "Due date must be today or a future date."
      },
      {
        "field": "assignee_id",
        "issue": "User usr_9z88x1 is not a member of this project."
      }
    ],
    "request_id": "req_c7a1d5e2f0"
  }
}
Field	Type	Description
error.code	string	A stable, machine-readable error identifier (e.g., invalid_json, unauthorized, validation_failed).
error.message	string	A human-readable summary of the problem.
error.details	array	Optional. Field-level problems, present for 400 and 422 errors.
error.request_id	string	A unique ID for the request. Include it when contacting support.

Notes
•	Idempotency: Always send an Idempotency-Key when retrying after a network timeout, to avoid creating duplicate tasks.
•	Time zones: due_date is a calendar date with no time zone. created_at and updated_at are always in UTC.
•	Assignee changes: To change an assignee after creation, use PATCH /v1/projects/{project_id}/tasks/{task_id}.

